---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import parameters from '../../generated/parameters.json';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const liveParameters = JSON.stringify(parameters);
---

<Base
  title="Modeling tool — Vermont School Budgets"
  description="Model what merging or closing schools would do to education spending and homestead tax rates, with every step of the arithmetic shown and cited."
>
  <h1>Modeling tool</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Every step of the weighted-membership and tax-rate arithmetic, shown and cited. Change the
    figures and watch each step change with them.
  </p>

  <div class="notice blocking">
    <strong>This tool cannot produce Vermont figures yet, and it will not pretend otherwise</strong>
    <p>
      No statutory parameter has been verified against current statute text, so on the live
      parameter set every step below reports what blocked it instead of showing a number. That is
      the engine working correctly: it refuses to compute from an unverified weight rather than
      returning a plausible one.
    </p>
    <p>
      Switch to the illustrative example to see what a completed walkthrough looks like. Its
      weights are deliberately arbitrary round numbers, and every step will say so.
    </p>
  </div>

  <form id="scenario-form">
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="field">
        <label for="parameter-mode">Parameter set</label>
        <select id="parameter-mode">
          <option value="live">Live — FY2027 (nothing verified yet)</option>
          <option value="example">Illustrative example (not Vermont law)</option>
        </select>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="example-warning" class="notice" hidden>
      <strong>These are not Vermont's pupil weights</strong>
      <p>
        The weights in this mode are arbitrary round numbers — a secondary weight of exactly 2, an
        economic deprivation weight of exactly 0.5 — chosen so the arithmetic is checkable by
        hand. They exist to demonstrate the shape of the calculation, not its result. Every
        parameter below carries the citation "SYNTHETIC TEST FIXTURE — not a statutory value and
        not Vermont law", so a figure copied out of this mode announces what it is.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Membership</h2>
    <p>
      Average daily membership by grade band, for two years. The statutory averaging rule decides
      how many years actually count.
    </p>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="field">
        <label for="prek-1">FY2025 prekindergarten</label>
        <input id="prek-1" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" value="10" />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="elem-1">FY2025 elementary</label>
        <input id="elem-1" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" value="100" />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="sec-1">FY2025 secondary</label>
        <input id="sec-1" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" value="50" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="field">
        <label for="prek-2">FY2026 prekindergarten</label>
        <input id="prek-2" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" value="20" />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="elem-2">FY2026 elementary</label>
        <input id="elem-2" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" value="200" />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="sec-2">FY2026 secondary</label>
        <input id="sec-2" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" value="100" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="controls">
      <div class="field">
        <label for="econ">Pupils at or below 185% FPL</label>
        <input id="econ" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" value="40" />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="el">English learner pupils</label>
        <input id="el" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" value="8" />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="sparsity"
          ><input id="sparsity" type="checkbox" /> Meets the sparsity test</label
        >
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="small-school"
          ><input id="small-school" type="checkbox" /> Meets the school size test</label
        >
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Spending and the town</h2>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="field">
        <label for="spending">Education spending ($)</label>
        <input id="spending" type="number" min="0" step="1000" value="3370000" />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="cla">Common level of appraisal</label>
        <input id="cla" type="number" min="0.1" max="2" step="0.0001" value="0.8" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </form>

  <h2>Result</h2>
  <div id="summary"></div>
  <div id="blockers"></div>

  <h2>Show your work</h2>
  <p>
    Every step of the calculation, in order, with what it did and why. This is the engine's own
    computation tree rendered directly — not a description of the arithmetic written separately
    from it, which could drift.
  </p>
  <div id="walkthrough"></div>

  <h2>Authorities used</h2>
  <div id="citations"></div>

  <h2>Assumptions register</h2>
  <p>
    Scenario assumptions and why each one defaults where it does. Every one is adjustable. Note
    in particular that consolidation defaults assume <em>no</em> reduction: any reduction shown is
    one you chose and can see, rather than one this tool assumed on your behalf.
  </p>
  <div id="assumptions"></div>

  <h2>What this tool will not do</h2>
  <p>
    It does not rank scenarios, score them, or describe any result as a saving. Changes are
    signed numbers presented in both directions. Transportation costs can be set to rise as well
    as fall, because consolidation frequently lengthens bus routes — a tool that only allowed that
    figure to fall would be modelling a conclusion rather than a system.
  </p>
  <p>
    Transition costs, construction aid, legacy debt incentives and transportation routing are out
    of scope and are not modelled. Where a position is assumed to be consolidated without a stated
    salary, the effect is reported as unknown rather than as zero.
  </p>
</Base>

<script define:vars={{ liveParameters }}>
  window.__VT_PARAMETERS__ = JSON.parse(liveParameters);
</script>

<script>
  import { initModelTool } from '../../scripts/model-tool';
  initModelTool(window.__VT_PARAMETERS__ ?? []);
</script>
